## Issue 3: Critical - Missing Error Handling for WASM Initialization

**Title:** `Critical: No error handling for WASM initialization failures`

**Labels:** `bug`, `priority:critical`

**Body:**
```markdown
## Problem

The `getSwe()` function in `src/lib/calculation/ephemeris.ts` has no error handling around WASM initialization, which can cause the entire API route to crash with uncaught promise rejections.

## Current Implementation (lines 22-35)

```typescript
async function getSwe(): Promise<SwissEPH> {
  if (!sweInstance) {
    const wasmPath = path.join(process.cwd(), 'public', 'swisseph.wasm');
    const wasmBuffer = readFileSync(wasmPath);  // ← Can throw
    const wasmBase64 = wasmBuffer.toString('base64');
    const wasmDataUrl = `data:application/wasm;base64,${wasmBase64}`;
    sweInstance = await SwissEPH.init(wasmDataUrl);  // ← Can reject
  }
  return sweInstance;
}
Failure Scenarios
Without error handling, these scenarios will crash:

File not found: If postinstall scripils, readFileSync throws
Network failures: If using HTTP URLs, fetch can fail
WASM compilation errors: Invalid or corrupted WASM file
Memory issues: Out of memory during initialization
Impact
API routes crash with 500 errors
No logging for debugging production issues
Poor user experience with generic error messages
Difficult to diagnose production failures
Recommended Solution
Add comprehensive error handling:

async function getSwe(): Promise<SwissEPH> {
  if (sweInstance) return sweInstance;

  try {
    // ... initialization code
    sweInstance = await SwissEPH.init(wasmUrl);
    return sweInstance;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Failed to initialize Swiss Ephemeris WASM:', error);
    throw new Error(
